description:
Problem: We need a lightweight, production-safe probing and traffic-slicing mechanism that detects function-call / structured-output incompatibilities between model versions during canary and A/B rollouts. Existing diff-only approaches flag many benign changes (naming, optional fields) and miss behavioral regressions where the schema superficially matches but semantics diverge. This ticket proposes a Contract-aware Traffic Slicer (CTS) and Function Interface Prober that augments schema diffs with execution fingerprints, semantic fuzz checks, and runtime failure heuristics to drive automated, bounded traffic slices and conditional auto-revert.

Goals:
- detect regressions that break downstream tool-calls or structured output consumers with both high precision and recall;
- limit blast radius via traffic slicing that routes only compatible request slices to the canary until confidence thresholds are met;
- provide clear telemetry and a deterministic auto-rollback policy for rapid mitigation.

Constraints: must work with hosted and Dedicated, respect customer-level routing policies (region/tier), and not add more than 5% p50 latency for canary slices. Must avoid any data exfiltration risk (no accidental routing of PII to shadow sinks).
